# Git commits: no Cursor co-author

Mandatory for all agent-created commits in this repository.

## Forbidden

- Never add `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` or any Cursor agent co-author line.
- Never add any `Co-authored-by:` trailer unless the user explicitly names a human co-author.
- Never use `git commit --trailer` for Cursor or any agent co-author.
- Never append co-author lines inside HEREDOC commit messages.

## Required

- Commit message body: subject and optional description only.
- Author: human user only.
- Before push: run `git log -1 --format=%B` and confirm no `Co-authored-by:` line exists.
- If a hook injects a Cursor co-author trailer, strip it before finishing the commit.
